================== ADDENDUM: k=11 CONFIRMATION + FLIP THRESHOLD ==================
Wider box [1..16] (8008 normalized sets, exhaustive): SAME argmax
  (0, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8, 10, 12, 14) -- interior extremal, not box-edge.
Structure: X = 2*consec_8  u  {3,5,7}   (the 2-dilated consecutive 8-set + odd infill).

Exact values:
  X:      p0 = 111/196  (~0.566327)   p1 = 167/840   (~0.198810)   Phi = 11159/17640 (~0.632596)
  consec: p0 = 3419/5880 (~0.581463)  p1 = 1283/8820 (~0.145465)   Phi = 33337/52920 (~0.629951)
  Phi(X) - Phi(consec) = 1/378 (~+0.002646)
  p0(consec) - p0(X)   = 89/5880 (consec REMAINS the p0-argmax: THM-534 intact)

FLIP THRESHOLD (exact): lambda*_11 = (p0(consec)-p0(X))/(p1(X)-p1(consec)) = 267/941 ~ 0.283741
  => kps cont.24's lambda* ladder 1.51 / 1.23 / 0.98 (k=8/9/10) continues DOWN through 1/3
     between k=10 and k=11: at lambda = 1/3 the joint argmax is NON-consec from k=11 on.

CONCLUSION: the "joint Phi-consec-extremality" lemma (kps cont.24's named remainder) is
FALSE as stated for k >= 11.  The recursion is UNAFFECTED: the needed inequality
Phi(F) <= cap_{|F|+1} holds in every box with margins +0.1196/+0.0856/+0.1142/+0.1583/
+0.2245 (k=7..11), the k=11 margin being the LARGEST.  The base lemma must target
Phi(F) <= cap_{|F|+1} directly (or consec-extremality restricted to k <= 10 + the
perforated-dilate family at k >= 11).  At the BINDING size k=8 (tightest margin),
consec IS the exact global argmax in the exhaustive box.
